### distilled skill library (.agent/ — successor to .omc/, renamed 2026-08-29) ###
# The distiller (hart-agent-homes/tools/distiller) writes $cwd/.agent/skills +
# skills-pending/ + .distiller/ into every repo an agent works in. Ignore the
# CONTENTS, never the `.agent` directory itself: hart's own .gitignore re-includes
# `.agent/skills/` as tracked, and excluding the directory here would silently stop
# git from descending into it.
**/.agent/*

# Sisyphus boulder state
.sisyphus/boulder.json


# zcode (Z.AI's coding CLI) writes an ACP sandbox config into every project it
# runs in: .zcode/acp/sandbox.json, two booleans, regenerated on each run. It is
# covered by no project .gitignore, so it shows up as untracked in every worktree
# an agent touches — three had appeared across ~/repos by 2026-09-14, including
# one in a repo slated to be published public. Harmless content, but a `git add -A`
# in an agent worktree would commit it.
.zcode/

# paseo writes per-workspace runtime state next to the project the same way.
.paseo/

# gjc writes generated workspace state next to the project.
.gjc/

# Deliberately NOT ignoring `.claude/` wholesale. Project .claude/ holds tracked
# content and a blanket rule would silently keep a newly authored skill out of
# `git status` rather than just hiding scratch. Surveyed 2026-09-14 across
# ~/repos: webfront alone TRACKS thirteen paths under .claude/ (agents, skills,
# commands, hooks, rules, conventions, analysis, references, reports, review,
# helpers, context-backup, settings.json), ollie_notes adds output-styles/, and
# telemetry tracks .claude/scheduled_tasks.json. The authored surface is both
# large and per-repo, so this is a denylist of the runtime artifacts instead.
# Add to it when a new one shows up; never invert it to a blanket ignore.
#
# Note the asymmetry on scheduled_tasks: the .json is authored (tracked in
# telemetry), the .lock beside it is runtime. Only the lock is ignored.
**/.claude/.credentials.json
**/.claude/scheduled_tasks.lock
**/.claude/memory.db
**/.claude/memory.db-wal
**/.claude/memory.db-shm
**/.claude/worktrees/
**/.claude/shell-snapshots/
**/.claude/history.jsonl
**/.claude/paste-cache/
**/.claude/file-history/
**/.claude/session-env/

# Not ignored on purpose, though they are runtime in ~/.claude: sessions/,
# projects/, ide/, cache/, debug/, tasks/. None has ever appeared inside a
# project .claude/ here, and .claude/sessions/ IS tracked in two vendored
# third-party repos under discord-chat-explorer/ — adding a rule for it would
